UnrealIRCd for Debian and Ubuntu (freshdeb)
===========================================

Getting started
---------------

The server doesn't start until it has a configuration. Start from upstream's
example, then follow https://www.unrealircd.org/docs/Configuration:

  cp /etc/unrealircd/examples/example.conf /etc/unrealircd/unrealircd.conf
  chgrp unrealircd /etc/unrealircd/unrealircd.conf
  chmod 0640 /etc/unrealircd/unrealircd.conf
  unrealircdctl gencloak          # cloak keys for set::cloak-keys
  unrealircdctl mkpasswd          # oper passwords
  runuser -u unrealircd -- unrealircd -c     # test the configuration
  systemctl start unrealircd

It runs as the user unrealircd, which can read /etc/unrealircd but not write
to it. The commands of upstream's "./unrealircd" script:

  ./unrealircd start|stop|restart    systemctl start|stop|restart unrealircd
  ./unrealircd rehash                unrealircdctl rehash (or systemctl reload)
  ./unrealircd reloadtls             unrealircdctl reloadtls
  ./unrealircd status                unrealircdctl status
  ./unrealircd configtest            runuser -u unrealircd -- unrealircd -c
  ./unrealircd mkpasswd|gencloak     unrealircdctl mkpasswd|gencloak
  ./unrealircd spkifp                unrealircdctl spkifp
  ./unrealircd version               runuser -u unrealircd -- unrealircd -v

Files
-----

  /etc/unrealircd/unrealircd.conf      yours (not shipped)
  /etc/unrealircd/*.default.conf,      upstream's defaults, links to
    *.optional.conf, help/, aliases/,  /usr/share/unrealircd/conf. Like
    examples/                          upstream's "make install", every
                                       upgrade replaces them: don't edit
                                       them, override them in your own files
  /etc/unrealircd/badwords.conf,       conffiles: yours to edit
    dccallow.conf, spamfilter.conf
  /etc/unrealircd/tls/                 server.cert.pem and server.key.pem,
                                       self-signed when the package was
                                       installed; replace them with your own.
                                       curl-ca-bundle.crt links to the
                                       system's CAs (ca-certificates)
  /var/lib/unrealircd                  data (databases, ircd.tune, the
                                       services MOTD)
  /var/cache/unrealircd                remote includes, GeoIP databases
  /var/log/unrealircd                  log files named in the configuration
  /usr/lib/unrealircd/modules          modules

Differences from upstream's installation
----------------------------------------

 * Upgrades come with apt, not "./unrealircd upgrade": the upgrade script,
   hot-patch and cold-patch aren't included. An upgrade restarts the server,
   as its modules are replaced and only load into the version they were
   built with.

 * When an advisory says to run "./unrealircd hot-patch <name>", install the
   release it comes with instead: upstream publishes each hot-patch together
   with a release that has the same fix, as the alternative for those who
   can't restart. That release reaches this repository like any other.

 * No third-party modules: the module manager ("./unrealircd module") isn't
   available. Modules compile against UnrealIRCd's configured source tree,
   which the package doesn't have, and have to be rebuilt for every release.
   If you need them, install UnrealIRCd from source instead.

 * The services MOTD (SVSMOTD) lives in /var/lib/unrealircd/ircd.svsmotd
   instead of the configuration directory, which the server can't write to.
   /ADDMOTD and /ADDOMOTD append to ircd.motd and oper.motd in
   /etc/unrealircd, so they fail; edit those files instead.

 * Built against the distribution's c-ares, PCRE2, argon2, libsodium and
   jansson instead of the copies upstream bundles, which get their security
   fixes from the distribution.

 * By default (modules.default.conf), the server downloads GeoIP databases
   from geoip.unrealircd.org every 14 days, as upstream's builds do; see
   https://www.unrealircd.org/docs/GeoIP to change that.
